{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","fileName":"src/bioetl/domain/composite/aggregation.py","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/bioetl/domain/composite/aggregation.py around lines 142 - 155, Update _try_comparison_operator to reject right-hand operands containing another supported comparison operator or boolean keyword, while preserving validation for exactly one comparison with non-empty operands. Keep _validate_comparison_filter limited to the existing == and != operators and ensure expressions such as chained comparisons or AND conditions return False or raise the established validation error.","suggestions":["def _try_comparison_operator(text: str, operator: str) -> bool:\n    if operator not in text:\n        return False\n    left, right = text.split(operator, 1)\n    _require_filter_field(left.strip())\n    value = right.strip()\n    if not value:\n        raise ValueError(\"aggregation filter_condition comparison requires a value\")\n    if \" == \" in value or \" != \" in value:\n        raise ValueError(\n            \"aggregation filter_condition supports a single comparison only\"\n        )\n    return True\n\n\ndef _validate_comparison_filter(text: str) -> bool:\n    if _try_comparison_operator(text, \" == \"):\n        return True\n    return _try_comparison_operator(text, \" != \")"]}
